VERDICT: FAIL
CHECKER: checker-second
FAMILY: adversarial
TASK: T15
ATTEMPT: 1
---
Scope reviewed: internal/handlers/whatif/handlers_sweep.go,
handlers_sweep_test.go, internal/templates/render_conversion_sweep_test.go,
web/templates/components/whatif/conversion-sweep.html, the route
registration in handlers.go, and the call graph into prepare/engine/analysis.

What I tried to break, and what happened:

1. Concurrency / shared mutable state — DID NOT BREAK.
   - candidateSettingsForConversionAmount does `cfg := *s` (shallow) then
     replaces only the RothConversion pointer with a fresh value — mirrors
     candidateSettingsForSS exactly (internal/services/retirement/analysis/
     tax_optimizer.go:63-75).
   - Each candidate goes through prepare.From -> DeepCopy, which is a full
     JSON marshal/unmarshal round trip (internal/services/retirement/
     prepare/prepare.go:80-93), not a pointer-preserving copy. That
     eliminates interior-pointer aliasing across the 9 concurrent
     eng.Run calls.
   - engine.Run is documented and, by inspection of runMonthlyLoop/stepper,
     behaves as a pure function of its Input; the only genuinely shared
     value across goroutines is baseIn.Chain/Hooks, which are read-only
     ([]PreparedChainLink, function value) built once outside the fan-out.
   - `go test -race -run ConversionSweep ./internal/handlers/whatif/...`
     found no race.
   - baseIn.Hooks is the zero-value engine.Hooks{} (buildEngineInput never
     populates it), which exactly matches the pre-existing precedent in
     handleWhatIfTaxOptimize (handlers_rates.go:483-489) — not a regression
     introduced by this task.

2. Candidate-amount insertion logic (0/25k/.../200k + current) — DID NOT
   BREAK. Verified via existing tests plus manual reasoning for current
   already-in-list, current above max, current below min (symmetric),
   nil RothConversion (defaults current to 0, already in list). Enabled
   follows `amount > 0` correctly, including the amount=0 case explicitly
   disabling (not leaving a stale Enabled=true) — TestCandidateSettings...
   EnabledFollowsAmount covers this.

3. Survives-vs-depletes rendering — DID NOT BREAK. Row and render tests
   isolate each row's own <tr>...</tr> markup (not just substring search
   in the whole document) so one row's content can't mask an assertion
   about the sibling row; both the handler-level split and the render-level
   split are exercised against a real engine-derived scenario, not a
   synthetic fixture.

4. Route/critical-globs/RunFull — DID NOT BREAK. `grep -n "RunFull\|
   MonteCarlo" handlers_sweep.go` only matches the doc comment explaining
   why the code deliberately avoids it; call graph is Load -> buildEngineInput
   (prepare.From only, confirmed by reading handlers.go:235-273) -> eng.Run.
   git status shows the changed/added files are handlers.go,
   handlers_sweep.go(+test), render_conversion_sweep_test.go,
   conversion-sweep.html, whatif.html — none match
   .swarm/critical.globs (storage/**, dataloader/**, retirement/engine/**,
   transfers/**, accounts/accounts.go, mcpsvc/confirm/**).

5. Page-load auto-fire — DID NOT BREAK. `git diff HEAD~1 -- web/templates/
   pages/whatif.html` shows exactly one added line, `{{template
   "whatif-conversion-sweep" .}}` (the button-only card), not the
   `-results` partial. TestRenderConversionSweep_ButtonState additionally
   asserts no `<table>` and no `hx-trigger="load"/"revealed"` in that
   template.

6. REAL DEFECT FOUND — Lifetime Tax column is mislabeled as real dollars.
   The template's caption (web/templates/components/whatif/
   conversion-sweep.html:76-81) states: "Ending balance and lifetime tax
   are in today's dollars; lifetime IRMAA is nominal, summed across
   projection years." This is factually wrong for the Lifetime Tax column.
   row.LifetimeTax is set from `analysis.BuildTax(proj, in).TotalTaxPaid`
   (handlers_sweep.go:114-116), which is an un-deflated sum of
   ProjectionYearSummary.Taxes across every year (tax.go:103-126) — it is
   NOT divided by CumulativeInflation anywhere in that path. I confirmed
   ys.Taxes itself is nominal by cross-referencing the sibling Tax
   Optimizer feature, which explicitly deflates the equivalent figure:
   `cand.LifetimeTaxReal += ys.Taxes / deflator` where
   `deflator := ys.CumulativeInflation` (tax_optimizer.go:239-241) — i.e.
   the codebase already has the "real" version of this exact quantity and
   the sweep does not use it, contradicting its own caption.
   I reproduced the magnitude with a throwaway test against
   sweepScenarioSettings() (the fixture the handler tests themselves use):
     nominal TotalTaxPaid=58836.03  real(deflated)=45722.73  ratio=1.287
   That is a 28.7% overstatement relative to what the caption claims the
   number represents — not a rounding-level discrepancy. A user reading
   "in today's dollars" and comparing Lifetime Tax against the correctly
   labeled real EndingBalanceReal column, or against the Tax Optimizer
   card's LifetimeTaxReal, is given a false apples-to-apples impression
   for the central financial figure this feature exists to produce.
   (Test file used to reproduce, then removed — not part of the shipped
   diff: internal/handlers/whatif/zz_sweep_check_test.go, content
   preserved in this session's scratchpad.)

   Note: acceptance criterion 5 in CONVERSION_SWEEP_SPEC.md literally says
   "lifetime tax: reuse analysis.BuildTax(proj, in) totals" — so using
   TotalTaxPaid does follow the letter of the spec. The defect is not
   "used the wrong field per spec," it is that the worker's own added UI
   copy asserts a units claim about that field that is false. The spec
   never asked for that caption sentence, and as written it misinforms the
   user about what they are looking at.

7. Accessibility (ACCESSIBILITY.md) — DID NOT BREAK on the points checked:
   #2 `<th scope="col">` present; #7/#12 dark-mode classes paired with light
   throughout; #8 "current" row uses a text badge, not color alone; #10
   focus moves to the swapped heading via hx-on::after-swap with
   tabindex="-1" and a visible focus ring; #15 spinner has
   `motion-reduce:animate-none`. No duplicate element IDs: the results
   partial does not re-render the `#conversion-sweep-panel` wrapper it is
   swapped into (only its inner contents via hx-swap="innerHTML").

Verdict rationale: six of seven attack surfaces held up under adversarial
pressure — this is solid work overall — but item 6 is a genuine, reproduced,
user-facing factual error about the units of the report's central financial
metric, in the feature's own added copy. Per the adversarial lane's mandate
to default to FAIL on ambiguity, and because this is exactly the class of
"real vs nominal dollars confusion" the dispatch explicitly asked me to
hunt for, I am failing this attempt. Fix is narrow: either deflate
LifetimeTax the way tax_optimizer.go does for LifetimeTaxReal, or correct
the caption to say "lifetime tax and lifetime IRMAA are nominal, summed
across projection years" and drop the "today's dollars" claim for tax.
